# Hami Legal App — Architecture (verified 2026-09-08)

> Every statement here was verified against the code on 2026-09-08.
> The previous version of this file described `App.tsx`, `DataService`, `AuthService`
> and `client`/`admin` screens — **none of which exist**. It was injected into every
> assisted request and actively misled the agents that worked on this repo.
> **If you change the architecture, update this file in the same commit.**

Iraqi legal case management for lawyers. Arabic RTL. Production-bound, handles
privileged case data. Phone-first (Capacitor), with a separate admin web app.

---

## ⛔ Hard constraints — never violate

1. **Zero Visual Freeze.** Do not change UI, colors, layout, fonts, spacing, or
   Tailwind classes without explicit per-change permission from the owner.
   Logic, performance, security, data integrity and code quality only.
2. **Never run a guard with `--save`.** It rewrites the ratchet baseline in
   `.audit/*.json` and makes CI green over a worse state. If a baseline genuinely
   must move, it goes in its own commit prefixed `baseline:` with the reason.
3. **Never delete a file just because nothing imports it.** Structural tests read
   source files by string path. Always `grep` the basename across `src`, `scripts`
   and `e2e` first.
4. **Never invent an API.** If a property or method you need does not exist, add it
   properly or use what exists — do not reach for it through
   `as unknown as { _something }`. A guard written against a non-existent
   `SecureStoreService._sessionUserId` silently killed seven save paths in this repo.
5. **No secrets in code, commits, or replies.** Report presence and location only.

