## Two apps, one repo

`__HAMI_CLIENT_PRODUCT__` is a build-time define that separates them.

### Product (phone / web) — the actual product
```
index.html
  → public/hami-boot.js          external, CSP-safe; paints the static shell
  → src/index.tsx                entry; arms local-only, boot paint cache, fonts
  → src/boot/*                   bootCriticalPreload, bootEntryPreamble,
                                 bootShellKickoff, bootStaleChunkReload,
                                 mountApplication, peekBootSessionUserId
  → src/app/AppBootRoot.tsx
  → src/app/AppResolvedRuntime.tsx
  → src/app/AppRuntimeShell.tsx  ← screen switch lives HERE
  → src/app/bootstrap/LawyerDashboardGate.tsx
  → src/app/runtime/*Loader.ts + *BootHydrator.ts + *InstantPaint*.ts
```

**Screens are state, not routes. There is no router.**
`AppRuntimeShell` switches exactly three: `'lawyer' | 'privacy' | 'support'`.
Everything else is an overlay/section inside the lawyer dashboard.

### Headquarters (HQ admin)
```
hq.html → src/hq/index.tsx → HqBootRoot → HqResolvedRuntime
```
Built with `vite build --mode hq` → `dist-hq`, deployed via `vercel-hq.json`.
`src/hq/stubs/*` alias out lawyer code so it never reaches the HQ bundle.

